 245:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   *
 246:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * The function generates 'size' equally spaced values in the closed interval [low,high].
 247:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * When size is set to 1, a vector of length 1 containing 'high' is returned.
 248:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   *
 249:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * \only_for_vectors
 250:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   *
 251:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * Example: \include DenseBase_LinSpaced.cpp
 252:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * Output: \verbinclude DenseBase_LinSpaced.out
 253:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   *
 254:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * For integer scalar types, an even spacing is possible if and only if the length of the range,
 255:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * i.e., \c high-low is a scalar multiple of \c size-1, or if \c size is a scalar multiple of the
 256:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * number of values \c high-low+1 (meaning each value can be repeated the same number of time).
 257:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * If one of these two considions is not satisfied, then \c high is lowered to the largest value
 258:Eigen/src/Core/CwiseNullaryOp.h ****   * satisfying one of this constraint.
